    "    pid_t pid = fork();",
    "    if (pid == 0) {  // Child process",
    "        printf(\"Child process executing\\n\");",
    "        return 0;  // Child exits",
    "    } else if (pid > 0) {  // Parent process",
    "        wait(NULL);  // Wait for child to finish",
    "        printf(\"Parent process resumes after child terminates\\n\");",
    "    } else {",
    "        printf(\"Fork failed\\n\");",
    "    }",
    "    return 0;",
    "}"
  ],
  "example_explanation": "This program uses fork() to create a child process, which prints a message and exits immediately. The parent process calls wait(NULL) to pause until the child terminates, then prints its own message. This demonstrates how wait() ensures the parent waits for the child, illustrating process synchronization."
}
